      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "IO::Uncompress::Unzip versions before 2.215 for Perl propagate uncaught exception when parsing zip header with malformed DOS date.  _dosToUnixTime() decodes the local-file-header last-modification date field and calls Time::Local::timelocal() without an eval guard. A header whose date field decodes to an out-of-range month, day, or hour causes timelocal() to die.  The exception propagates out of IO::Uncompress::Unzip->new($file) where callers expect undef plus $UnzipError.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
